`\rowcolor` is provided by the **xcolor** package with the **table** option (or by `colortbl`). It colors the background of an entire row in a `tabular`/`array`.

### Minimal example
```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor} % provides \rowcolor

\begin{document}

\begin{tabular}{lcr}
\rowcolor{gray!25}
A & B & C \\
1 & 2 & 3 \\
\rowcolor{yellow!30}
x & y & z \\
\end{tabular}

\end{document}
```

### Notes / common usage
- Place `\rowcolor{<color>}` **immediately before** the row you want to color.
- Colors can be predefined (`red`, `blue`, etc.) or mixed (`gray!20`, `blue!10`).
- If you also want alternating row colors automatically, use:
  ```latex
  \rowcolors{2}{gray!10}{white}
  ```
  (also from `xcolor` with `table`).

If you tell me whether you’re using `tabular`, `longtable`, or something like `tabularx`, I can tailor an example (including header coloring, alternating rows, etc.).

